    {
      "@id": "#specimen-imaging-preparation-protocol-idr0108-sabinina-nuclearporecomplex-experimenta",
      "@type": "bia:SpecimenImagingPreparationProtocol",
      "name": "Specimen imaging preparation protocol",
      "description": "U2OS cells were cultured at 37C and 5% CO2 in 1x high glucose McCoy's 5A modified medium with 10% (v/v) fetal bovine serum, 100 U/ml penicillin-streptomycin, 2 mM L-glutamin, 1 mM sodium pyruvate and 1% MEM nonessential amino acid. Tests confirming the absence of mycoplasma were performed every 2 months.\n\nThe nucleoporin gene of interest was edited with the SNAPf-tag Zinc finger nucleases to add a SNAP tag at the N-terminus of the protein. Tagged proteins were detected using benzylguanine-conjugated AF647 and ELYS with a polyclonal rabbit antibody followed by a secondary antibody coupled to CF680. Data was acquired on a custom-built wide-field setup described in Deschamps et al., 2016 using a cylindrical lens (f = 1000 mm) to introduce astigmatism.\n\nBlinking event data (files with names MMStack*.ome.tif)  was processed to generate localization data (in csv files) which was further processed to produce the final images (files with names sml_3Dvolume*.tif). Processing was done with the SMAP software (https://github.com/jries/SMAP)"
    },
    {
